cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this design, please cite it as below."
title: "1 GSPS Digital-Throughput 8192-point Real-Time Spectrum Analyser on Artix-7"
abstract: >-
  A complete RTL implementation of a real-time spectrum analyser for digital
  baseband IQ signals on a single Artix-7 XC7A35T-FGG484-2. Four parallel
  2048-point streaming FFT cores are merged on the output side by a radix-4
  butterfly into an 8192-point spectrum, giving 1 GSPS digital throughput at
  250 MHz with four complex samples per clock. A bit-exact 3-multiplication
  Karatsuba complex multiplier reduces the multiplier budget from 105 to 85
  DSP48E1 slices, which is what makes four parallel lanes fit. The stimulus is
  an on-chip ROM replay; there is no high-speed ADC and no analogue front end,
  so the throughput figure is a digital-domain property.
